# ClubDay

ClubDay is a campus club-day platform for student check-in, attendance, and certificates.
Organizers run events; students scan in, get marked present, and later download certificates.
Treat every change as production-bound: validate input, enforce policy on the server, and keep check-in fast.

## Stack

Next.js App Router, TypeScript, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Motion, Drizzle, Better Auth, Supabase, Vitest, Playwright, k6.

## Folder layout

- `src/app` — App Router pages and route handlers
- `src/components` — UI components
- `src/db` — Drizzle schema, client, and migrations (all database access)
- `src/lib` — shared helpers (including `policy.ts`)
- `src/server` — server-only logic
- `scripts` — one-off and seed scripts
- `tests` — Vitest and Playwright tests
- `load` — k6 load tests

## Conventions

- Server actions and route handlers validate input with Zod.
- All database access goes through `src/db`.
- Every mutation calls `can()` from `src/lib/policy.ts` on the server.
- Store times in UTC; display them in `Asia/Kolkata`.
- Read environment variables only through `src/env.ts`.

## Hard rules

- Never trust a user id or role sent by the client.
- Never log tokens or secrets.
- Never commit `.env` files.
- The student check-in endpoint must stay one database round trip.
- Every new feature needs a Vitest or Playwright test.

## Workflow

- Work in small steps.
- Run lint, typecheck, and tests before saying a task is done.
- Tell the user what to commit; do not commit unless asked.
